# Build-context exclusions for the eduLLM platform image build.
#
# The platform builds .edullm/Dockerfile with the repository root as the context, so this
# is the file Docker consults: the build client reads .dockerignore from the root of the
# context, never from the directory holding the Dockerfile, which is why a
# .edullm/.dockerignore would be silently inert. Patterns match against the whole
# context-relative path rather than gitignore-style at any depth, so anything that has to
# match below the root carries an explicit **/ prefix.

# actions/checkout leaves the run's token in .git/config, and the context is the
# repository root. Dropping .git here keeps both that credential and the repository
# history out of the context altogether, so no COPY in this or any future revision of the
# Dockerfile can reach them.
.git

# .git is the only tracked-or-present path this file removes on purpose. Everything below
# names something this repository does not track, so excluding it takes no source out of
# the image; it stops a local build from absorbing developer state that the clean
# checkout CI builds from would never have.

# Python bytecode and packaging artefacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
pip-wheel-metadata

# Virtual environments and local worktrees
**/.venv
**/venv
.worktrees

# Tool caches and test output
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.benchmarks
.coverage
**/.ipynb_checkpoints

# Editor and operating system artefacts
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
**/*.swp

# Local training output and caches
runs
wandb
scratch
dataset-cache
docs/build
site
